        </div>

        <div class="section-title">Page 1: Conducting Portion &amp; Nasal Cavity Framework</div>

        <div class="question-box">
            <div class="question-text">1. Which of the following functional combinations correctly lists all primary responsibilities of the conducting portion?</div>
            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item correct-answer"><strong>A)</strong> Filtering, moistening, warming, and conducting air</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>B)</strong> Gas exchange, surfactant synthesis, and blood filtration</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>C)</strong> Detoxification, endocrine secretion, and gas distribution</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>D)</strong> Exclusively warming and oxygenating the systemic arterial blood</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="question-box">
            <div class="question-text">2. Which anatomical structure is histologically classified as the final component of the conducting portion?</div>
            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item"><strong>A)</strong> Respiratory bronchiole</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>B)</strong> Alveolar duct</div>
                <div class="option-item correct-answer"><strong>C)</strong> Terminal bronchiole</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>D)</strong> Segmental tertiary bronchus</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="question-box">
            <div class="question-text">3. When moving deeper into the nasal vestibule, how does the lining epithelium transform before becoming respiratory epithelium?</div>
            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item"><strong>A)</strong> Simple cuboidal to stratified columnar ciliated</div>
                <div class="option-item correct-answer"><strong>B)</strong> Stratified squamous keratinized to stratified squamous non-keratinized</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>C)</strong> Pseudopodia-bearing simple squamous to transient columnar</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>D)</strong> Transitional epithelium directly to stratified squamous keratinized</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="question-box">
            <div class="question-text">4. Which morphological features are distinctively localized within the sub-epithelium and skin of the nasal vestibule?</div>
            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item"><strong>A)</strong> Multi-lamellar bodies and diffuse Clara cells</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>B)</strong> Purely serous Kulchitsky cells and deep hyaline plates</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>C)</strong> Highly organized C-shaped elastic cartilage framework</div>
                <div class="option-item correct-answer"><strong>D)</strong> Vibrissae (thick short hairs), sweat glands, and sebaceous glands</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="question-box">
            <div class="question-text">5. What is the precise histological definition and function of "Swell Bodies" within the nasal fossae lamina propria?</div>
            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item correct-answer"><strong>A)</strong> Large venous plexuses in the conchae that periodically engorge to warm inspired air</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>B)</strong> Lymphatic aggregations that synthesize protective surfactants locally</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>C)</strong> Specialized sensory corpuscles responding to olfactory chemical changes</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>D)</strong> Mucus-secreting epithelial invaginations lacking a clear basal lamina</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="question-box">
            <div class="question-text">6. Which specific part of the nasal cavity framework is lined by specialized Olfactory Epithelium instead of standard respiratory epithelium?</div>
            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item"><strong>A)</strong> Inferior nasal concha</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>B)</strong> Middle nasal concha</div>
                <div class="option-item correct-answer"><strong>C)</strong> Superior nasal concha</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>D)</strong> Entire floor of the nasal fossae</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="question-box">
            <div class="question-text">7. Histologically, how is the mucosal membrane of the paranasal sinuses uniquely arranged against its underlying support?</div>
            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item"><strong>A)</strong> Separated from bone by a thick, highly vascularized muscularis mucosae layer</div>
                <div class="option-item correct-answer"><strong>B)</strong> Fused directly with the underlying periosteum of the cranial bones</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>C)</strong> Free-floating without attachments, forming transient structural air folds</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>D)</strong> Anchored exclusively by dense elastic sheets to regional striated skeletal fibers</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="question-box">
            <div class="question-text">8. Which type of lining epithelium protects the Oropharynx and Laryngopharynx against mechanical frictional wear?</div>
            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item"><strong>A)</strong> Pseudostratified ciliated columnar epithelium</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>B)</strong> Simple columnar epithelium with specialized brush borders</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>C)</strong> Stratified squamous keratinized epithelium</div>
                <div class="option-item correct-answer"><strong>D)</strong> Stratified squamous non-keratinized epithelium</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="footer-wrapper">
            <div class="key-banner">
                ANSWER KEY 📍 Q1: A | Q2: C | Q3: B | Q4: D | Q5: A | Q6: C | Q7: B | Q8: D
            </div>
