        <div class="question-box">
            <div class="question-text">29. What is the classical structural appearance and distribution percentage of Type II pneumocytes?</div>
            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item correct-answer"><strong>A)</strong> Cuboidal cells with central round nuclei that cover only about 5% of the surface area but are numerically frequent</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>B)</strong> Extremely thinned squamous profiles covering 95% of the absolute surface area lines</div>
