        <div class="question-box">
            <div class="question-text">30. Which characteristic cytoplasmic organelle/inclusion body is found inside Type II pneumocytes?</div>
            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item"><strong>A)</strong> Large crystalline elementary particles rich in hemosiderin rings</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>B)</strong> Abundant zymogen vacuoles containing raw proteolytic trypsin complexes</div>
                <div class="option-item correct-answer"><strong>C)</strong> Multilamellar bodies containing phospholipid sheets of newly synthesized surfactant</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>D)</strong> Melanosome grids structurally organized along parallel tubule rows</div>
