            <div class="options-container">
                <div class="option-item"><strong>A)</strong> Destroying old red blood cells and storing iron molecules safely inside the lung septa</div>
                <div class="option-item correct-answer"><strong>B)</strong> Phagocytosing/recycling surfactant and dividing to regenerate both themselves and Type I pneumocytes</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>C)</strong> Building the collagenous bundles that create the outer visceral pleural layer sheets</div>
                <div class="option-item"><strong>D)</strong> Serving as structural contracting cells that physically shrink alveoli during coughing episodes</div>
            </div>
        </div>

